.md
## Dynamic Example
Firstly we need to optimize the rendering of our canvas. It can be done by utilizing a single buffer array used by all polygons on a canvas. If new polygons were added, we can append a new dynamic polygon directly to the graphics canvas using `FrontSubmit`, which kinda evaluates a symbol inside an instance of `Graphics`

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Dynamic Example
Firstly we need to optimize the rendering of our canvas. It can be done by utilizing a single buffer array used by all polygons on a canvas. If new polygons were added, we can append a new dynamic polygon directly to the graphics canvas using `FrontSubmit`, which kinda evaluates a symbol inside an instance of `Graphics`

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  InitGroup: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
applyDiffs[buffer_, old_, new_, raw_, scene_] := Module[{
  newBuffer = Join[buffer, Table[{}, {i, Length[new]-Length[old]}]],
  k
},
  MapIndexed[Function[{value, index}, With[{i = index[[1]]},
    newBuffer[[i]] = value[[1]]; 
  ]], old];

  For[k = Length[old], k < Length[new], k++, 
    newBuffer[[k+1]] = new[[k+1,1]];
  ];

  buffer = newBuffer;
  
  For[k = Length[old], k < Length[new], k++,  With[{u=k+1},
    FrontSubmit[{raw[[u,3]], Polygon[buffer[[u]]//Offload]}, scene]
  ]];
]

SetAttributes[applyDiffs, HoldFirst];

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
For the rest we only need to listern to the events of a cursor and recalculate all polygons as usual

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
For the rest we only need to listern to the events of a cursor and recalculate all polygons as usual

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: false
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
scene = FrontInstanceReference[];
rawDrops = {};

drops = {};
buffer = {};
drawing = Null;
streams = {};

cell; 

calc := With[{},
      With[{newDrops = combLine[dripDrops[{},rawDrops[[All,1]], rawDrops[[All,2]]], streams[[All,1]], streams[[All,2]], 2., 0.3]},
        applyDiffs[buffer, drops, newDrops, rawDrops, scene];
        drops = newDrops;
      ]
]

With[{}, cell = ResultCell[]; Graphics[{
  EventHandler[Null, {
    "click" -> Function[xy,
      rawDrops = Append[rawDrops, {xy, RandomReal[{0.1,0.9}], ColorData[37][RandomInteger[{1,50}]]}];
      
      calc;
      calc;
      (*Beep[];*)
      drawing = Null;
    ],

    "altclick" -> Function[xy,
      If[ListQ[drawing] == True,
        streams = Append[streams, {drawing, Normalize[xy - drawing]}];
        calc;
        calc;
        drawing = Null;
      ,
        drawing = xy;
      ];    
      
    ]
  }],

  scene
}, "TransitionDuration"->150, PlotRange->{{-5,5}, {-5,5}}, Controls->False, ImagePadding->None] ]

